{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>You shall begin to count seven weeks.</b> One must know why He repeated, saying ״תִּסְפֹּר שִׁבְעָה שָׁבֻעוֹת״? And perhaps it is because He means to tell them: even if no sickle arose to begin with it and it came from the loft (Menachot 83b), nevertheless you shall begin to count seven weeks. And this is according to the one who says (most halakhic authorities) that the counting of the Omer in our time is by rabbinic decree. But according to the one who says (Rambam) it is biblical, the verse repeated for our time." "<b>Thus concludes the portion Re'eh.</b>"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:17:37.058765974Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}